<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/alexandria-old-town.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/alexandria-old-town-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/alexandria-old-town.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/virginia-localities/">Localities</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Alexandria</span></nav><p class="kicker">Northern Virginia</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Alexandria, VA</h1><p class="lede">Alexandria’s Old Town holds some of the oldest homes in the country, a few blocks from the Potomac. Claims here are about original materials and the cost to restore them.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Locality</dt><dd>Independent city (no county)</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Northern Virginia</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips chips-dark"><li>Potomac tidal flooding</li><li>Flash flooding</li><li>Fallen trees</li><li>Fire</li><li>Wind</li></ul><p class="note-small"><b>Housing mix:</b> 18th- and 19th-century Old Town rowhouses, Del Ray bungalows, high-rise and mid-rise condos.</p></div>
<h2>Old Town and beyond</h2>
<p>Alexandria is an independent city on the Potomac River just south of Arlington. Old Town’s brick and frame rowhouses date to the 18th and 19th centuries and sit in one of the oldest historic districts in the country, governed by the city’s Board of Architectural Review. Del Ray and Rosemont offer early-1900s bungalows and foursquares. Seminary Hill, Beverly Hills and the West End add mid-century homes, while Potomac Yard and Carlyle bring newer mid-rise and high-rise condos.</p>
<h2>Storm history</h2>
<p>Old Town’s waterfront floods when strong winds push water up the Potomac. Hurricane Isabel in 2003 put several feet of water into lower King Street and the blocks nearby. Summer downpours in recent years have also caused flash flooding in Del Ray and along Four Mile Run. The 2012 derecho downed trees throughout the city.</p>
<h2>Common disputes in Alexandria</h2>
<ul>
<li>Plaster on lath, wide-plank floors and handmade millwork priced as modern materials.</li>
<li>Board of Architectural Review requirements for windows, roofing and exterior finishes.</li>
<li>Fire losses in attached rowhouses that spread smoke through party walls.</li>
<li>Water losses in condos and converted older buildings.</li>
<li>Basement water losses limited by backup sub-limits or flood exclusions.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Ordinance-or-law coverage</h2>
<p>When review-board rules require slate, wood windows or original-style trim, the added cost may fall under your policy’s ordinance-or-law coverage instead of the basic dwelling coverage. We check that limit before pricing the work, so the estimate matches what the policy can pay. See our <a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/historic-home-claim-appraisal/">historic home appraisal</a> service for more.</p>
<h2>Services available in Alexandria</h2><p>Every Virginia Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Alexandria and the surrounding area, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/commercial-and-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/hail-and-roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/windstorm-and-tornado-appraisal/">Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/hurricane-and-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/fire-and-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul><h2>Questions from Alexandria property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does the Board of Architectural Review affect my insurance claim?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It can raise repair costs if approved materials are required. Whether the policy pays the difference usually depends on ordinance-or-law coverage and its limit.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is an insurance appraiser in Alexandria useful for condo claims?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Condo claims often turn on which policy covers which part of the loss. We review both policies before valuing the disputed items.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby localities</h2><div class="related"><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-arlington-va/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Arlington</span></a><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-fairfax-va/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Fairfax County</span></a><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-fredericksburg-va/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Fredericksburg</span></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a><p class="box-small">Mon–Fri 8am–6pm ET · All of Virginia</p></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">Virginia localities</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-virginia-beach-va/">Virginia Beach, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-norfolk-va/">Norfolk, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-chesapeake-va/">Chesapeake, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-newport-news-va/">Newport News, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-richmond-va/">Richmond, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-arlington-va/">Arlington</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-alexandria-va/" aria-current="page">Alexandria, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-fairfax-va/">Fairfax County</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-fredericksburg-va/">Fredericksburg, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-charlottesville-va/">Charlottesville, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-roanoke-va/">Roanoke, VA</a></li><li><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-lynchburg-va/">Lynchburg, VA</a></li></ul></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">Free tools</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/calculators-for-policyholders/claim-gap-and-fee-estim